diff --git a/features/filtering.feature b/features/filtering.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2a405a8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/filtering.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,121 @@
+Feature: Filtering and controls
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want to filter todos by status and use bulk controls
+  So that I can focus on relevant tasks and manage them efficiently
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Toggle all
+
+    Scenario: Toggle all marks every todo as completed
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user toggles the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
+      And the todo "Walk dog" has the completed class
+      And the todo count shows "0 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Toggle all reflects state when all todos are individually completed
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user toggles the todo "Walk dog"
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle all reflects state when some todos are active
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+    Scenario: Toggle all unchecking unmarks all todos
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the user toggles the toggle-all checkbox
+      When the user toggles the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" does not have the completed class
+      And the todo "Walk dog" does not have the completed class
+
+  Rule: Counter
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows correct count for active todos
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the user has created a todo "Write spec"
+      When the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo count shows "2 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter pluralizes correctly for one item
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo count shows "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Counter shows zero items when all are completed
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo count shows "0 items left"
+
+  Rule: Clear completed
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed removes completed todos
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user clicks the clear-completed button
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is not in the list
+      And the todo "Walk dog" is in the list
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed button is hidden when no todos are completed
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+    Scenario: Clear completed button is visible when some todos are completed
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the clear-completed button is visible
+
+  Rule: Route filtering
+
+    Scenario: All route shows all todos
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user navigates to "#/"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is in the list
+      And the todo "Walk dog" is in the list
+      And the "All" filter is selected
+
+    Scenario: Active route shows only uncompleted todos
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is not in the list
+      And the todo "Walk dog" is in the list
+      And the "Active" filter is selected
+
+    Scenario: Completed route shows only completed todos
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is in the list
+      And the todo "Walk dog" is not in the list
+      And the "Completed" filter is selected
+
+    Scenario: Default route is all when no hash is present
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user navigates to ""
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is in the list
+      And the todo "Walk dog" is in the list
+      And the "All" filter is selected
+
+    Scenario: Toggling a todo in a filtered view updates the list
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is not in the list
+      And the todo count shows "1 item left"
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9296a55
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+Feature: Persistence
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want my todos to survive page reloads
+  So that I do not lose my work
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: localStorage persistence
+
+    Scenario: Todos persist across page reload
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is in the list
+      And the todo "Walk dog" is in the list
+      And the todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
+      And the todo "Walk dog" does not have the completed class
+      And the todo count shows "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Completed state persists across reload
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
+
+    Scenario: Active filter persists across reload
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      And the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user navigates to "#/active"
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the "Active" filter is selected
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is not in the list
+      And the todo "Walk dog" is in the list
diff --git a/features/todo-editing.feature b/features/todo-editing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6208e9e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-editing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+Feature: Todo editing
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want to edit existing todo titles inline
+  So that I can correct or update what needs to be done
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: Activating edit mode
+
+    Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label activates edit mode
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user double-clicks the todo label "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" has the editing class
+      And the edit input for "Buy milk" has focus
+
+    Scenario: Edit input contains the current todo title
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user double-clicks the todo label "Buy milk"
+      Then the edit input value is "Buy milk"
+
+  Rule: Saving an edit
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Enter saves the edited title
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user is editing the todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user changes the edit input to "Buy cookies" and presses Enter
+      Then the todo "Buy cookies" is in the list
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is not in the list
+      And the todo "Buy cookies" does not have the editing class
+
+    Scenario: Blurring the edit input saves the title
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user is editing the todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user changes the edit input to "Buy cookies" and blurs
+      Then the todo "Buy cookies" is in the list
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is not in the list
+
+    Scenario: Saving trims whitespace from the title
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user is editing the todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user changes the edit input to "  Buy cookies  " and presses Enter
+      Then the todo "Buy cookies" is in the list
+
+    Scenario: Saving an empty title removes the todo
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user is editing the todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user clears the edit input and presses Enter
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is not in the list
+
+  Rule: Cancelling an edit
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Escape discards changes
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user is editing the todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user changes the edit input to "Buy cookies" and presses Escape
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is in the list
+      And the todo "Buy cookies" is not in the list
+      And the todo "Buy milk" does not have the editing class
diff --git a/features/todo-lifecycle.feature b/features/todo-lifecycle.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0cfe868
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todo-lifecycle.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+Feature: Todo lifecycle
+  As a user managing tasks
+  I want to create, toggle, and delete todos
+  So that I can track what needs to be done
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Rule: New todos
+
+    Scenario: Creating a todo from the input
+      When the user types "Buy milk" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      Then a todo item "Buy milk" appears in the list
+      And the new-todo input is empty
+      And the todo count shows "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Trims whitespace from new todo input
+      When the user types "  Buy milk  " in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      Then a todo item "Buy milk" appears in the list
+
+    Scenario: Does not create a todo from empty input
+      When the user presses Enter in the new-todo input
+      Then no todo items appear in the list
+
+    Scenario: Does not create a todo from whitespace-only input
+      When the user types "   " in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      Then no todo items appear in the list
+
+    Scenario: The new-todo input is focused on page load
+      Then the new-todo input has focus
+
+  Rule: Completing a todo
+
+    Scenario: Toggling a todo marks it completed
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      When the user toggles the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
+      And the todo count shows "0 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Uncompleted todo has no completed class
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" does not have the completed class
+
+  Rule: Deleting a todo
+
+    Scenario: Deleting a todo removes it from the list
+      Given the user has created a todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user has created a todo "Walk dog"
+      When the user deletes the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" is not in the list
+      And the todo "Walk dog" is in the list
+
+  Rule: Main and footer visibility
+
+    Scenario: Main section and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+      Then the main section is hidden
+      And the footer is hidden
+
+    Scenario: Main section and footer appear when a todo is created
+      When the user types "Buy milk" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      Then the main section is visible
+      And the footer is visible
